            "location": "context",
            "explanation": "This statement collects signal handling information (SIG_IGN and SIG_CATCH) from the task structure without proper synchronization. In the context of /proc filesystem exposure, reading signal disposition data from task_struct can create race conditions where the task may exit or modify its signal handlers while being read, potentially leading to use-after-free or information disclosure vulnerabilities. The absence of proper locking when accessing sig->sigaction arrays allows concurrent modifications during the read operation."
